data
  title Two env-var regimes: one crashes, one leaks forever
  desc The one-prefix rename that turns a crash into a permanent leak
  compares
    - label Server var
      children
        - label process.env.SECRET — a server var
        - label Read at runtime, on the server
        - label In a client bundle: just undefined
        - label A crash or silent fail, never a leak
        - label Rotate anytime, no rebuild needed
    - label Public var
      children
        - label NEXT_PUBLIC_SECRET — a public var
        - label Inlined as a string literal at build time
        - label Readable by every visitor in devtools
        - label Rotation needs a rebuild and redeploy
        - label Shipped once equals compromised forever
